<section class="firewall-lab">
    <h2>🛠️ Lab Setup: Firewall Rule Audit & Attack Simulation</h2>
    <p class="intro-text">
        This lab will teach you how to audit firewall rules and simulate real-world attacks to test your network security.
    </p>

    <div class="setup-step">
        <div class="step-header">
            <span class="step-number">1</span>
            <h3>Build Your Security Lab</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
            <div class="instruction-card">
                <div class="instruction-icon">💻</div>
                <div class="instruction-text">
                    Create a new GNS3 project named: <span class="highlight">ALab1</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="visual-guide">
                <p><strong>Add these devices:</strong></p>
                <div class="device-grid">
                    <div class="device-item">
                        <div class="device-icon">🛡️</div>
                        <div>pfSense Firewall</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="device-item">
                        <div class="device-icon">🖥️</div>
                        <div>2 Windows PCs</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="device-item">
                        <div class="device-icon">🐧</div>
                        <div>Kali Linux</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="device-item">
                        <div class="device-icon">🔄</div>
                        <div>1 Router</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="device-item">
                        <div class="device-icon">🔀</div>
                        <div>2 Switches</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="connection-guide">
                <p><strong>Network Layout:</strong></p>
                <div class="connection-visual">
                    <div class="connection-line">
                        <span>Internet (Cloud)</span> <span class="arrow">→</span> <span>pfSense WAN</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="connection-line">
                        <span>pfSense LAN</span> <span class="arrow">→</span> <span>Switch1</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="connection-line">
                        <span>Switch1</span> <span class="arrow">→</span> <span>Windows PCs</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="connection-line">
                        <span>pfSense DMZ</span> <span class="arrow">→</span> <span>Switch2</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="connection-line">
                        <span>Switch2</span> <span class="arrow">→</span> <span>Kali Linux</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="note-box">
                <div class="note-icon">💡</div>
                <div class="note-text">
                    <strong>Security Zones:</strong> We're creating three zones - WAN (Internet), LAN (Trusted), and DMZ (Semi-Trusted)
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
        <div class="step-header">
            <span class="step-number">2</span>
            <h3>Configure Firewall Rules</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
            <div class="instruction-card important">
                <div class="instruction-icon">⌨️</div>
                <div class="instruction-text">
                    Access pfSense web interface at <span class="highlight">https://192.168.1.1</span> (default creds: admin/pfsense)
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="config-section">
                <div class="device-config">
                    <h4>Basic Rule Setup</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">Firewall → Rules → LAN:</div>
                        <code>
                            Action: Pass
                            Interface: LAN
                            Protocol: TCP
                            Source: LAN net
                            Destination: Any
                            Port: Any
                            Description: Allow LAN to Internet
                        </code>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="device-config">
                    <h4>DMZ Restrictions</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">Firewall → Rules → DMZ:</div>
                        <code>
                            Action: Pass
                            Interface: DMZ
                            Protocol: TCP
                            Source: DMZ net
                            Destination: LAN net
                            Port: 80,443
                            Description: Limited DMZ access
                        </code>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="note-box warning">
                <div class="note-icon">⚠️</div>
                <div class="note-text">
                    <strong>Default Deny:</strong> Remember pfSense blocks all traffic by default. Only what you explicitly allow will pass.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
        <div class="step-header">
            <span class="step-number">3</span>
            <h3>Attack Simulation Tests</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
            <div class="instruction-card important">
                <div class="instruction-icon">🐧</div>
                <div class="instruction-text">
                    Use Kali Linux to simulate attacks from the DMZ
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="test-instructions">
                <h4>Three Attack Simulations</h4>

                <div class="test-case">
                    <div class="test-number">1</div>
                    <div class="test-content">
                        <p><strong>Port Scanning (Reconnaissance):</strong></p>
                        <div class="code-block">
                            <code>nmap -sS 192.168.1.0/24</code>
                            <span class="comment"># Check what ports are visible from DMZ</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="expected-output">
                            <p><strong>Audit Check:</strong> Only necessary ports should be visible</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="test-case">
                    <div class="test-number">2</div>
                    <div class="test-content">
                        <p><strong>SQL Injection Attempt:</strong></p>
                        <div class="code-block">
                            <code>sqlmap -u "http://192.168.1.100/login.php" --risk=3 --level=5</code>
                            <span class="comment"># Test web application filtering</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="expected-output">
                            <p><strong>Audit Check:</strong> WAF should block suspicious patterns</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="test-case">
                    <div class="test-number">3</div>
                    <div class="test-content">
                        <p><strong>ICMP Flood (DDoS Test):</strong></p>
                        <div class="code-block">
                            <code>hping3 --flood --rand-source --icmp 192.168.1.1</code>
                            <span class="comment"># Test flood protection</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="expected-output">
                            <p><strong>Audit Check:</strong> Firewall should throttle/block excessive ICMP</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="note-box tip">
                <div class="note-icon">📊</div>
                <div class="note-text">
                    <strong>Log Analysis:</strong> Check pfSense logs after each test (Status → System Logs → Firewall)
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
        <div class="step-header">
            <span class="step-number">4</span>
            <h3>Rule Optimization</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
            <div class="instruction-card">
                <div class="instruction-icon">🛡️</div>
                <div class="instruction-text">
                    Based on test results, refine your firewall rules
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="config-section">
                <div class="device-config">
                    <h4>Recommended Improvements</h4>
                    <ul class="improvement-list">
                        <li>Create explicit deny rules before your allow rules</li>
                        <li>Enable pfBlockerNG for IP reputation filtering</li>
                        <li>Set up Snort/Suricata for IPS functionality</li>
                        <li>Schedule regular rule audits</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="device-config">
                    <h4>Example Secure Rule</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">Firewall → Rules → WAN:</div>
                        <code>
                            Action: Block
                            Interface: WAN
                            Protocol: Any
                            Source: !LAN net
                            Destination: LAN net
                            Log: Yes
                            Description: Explicit deny all
                        </code>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="completion-message success">
        <h3>🎉 Firewall Audit Complete!</h3>
        <p>You've successfully tested your firewall against real-world attack scenarios!</p>
        <div class="next-steps">
            <p><strong>Challenge:</strong> Try configuring geo-blocking rules to restrict by country!</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

